IMPORT prelude

-- Registration of Deeds Act 1988 (Singapore) -- caveats, priority, tacking: ss 8, 14, 15 and 16.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Registration of Deeds Act 1988 -- caveats and priority`

§§ `8 -- caveats`

-- s 8(1): a caveat may be (a) GIVEN by the proprietor for an estate or interest in favour of a named person, or
-- (b) LODGED by a person CLAIMING an estate or interest.
-- s 8(4): the Registrar "must not register" a caveat that (a) does not disclose any estate or interest in land, or
-- (b) does not state the Government survey lot number (or, for part of a lot, identify the part in a plan).
-- s 8(5): if after provisional registration the Registrar finds non-compliance, the Registrar MAY cancel.
-- s 8(6): "Despite subsections (4) and (5), the Registrar must not be concerned to consider whether or not a
-- caveator's claim is justified."
-- s 8(7): a person lodging a caveat as a claimant must serve notice by registered post on the proprietor and all
-- persons with prior claims on the register, "and the Registrar must not be concerned to inquire whether or not the
-- notice has been effected."
-- s 8(9): a registered caveat is "unless withdrawn by the caveator or cancelled by an order of court, in force for a
-- period of 5 years."
--
-- So the claimant's only protection against a groundless caveat is a court order; the Registrar does not test the
-- claim and does not check that the proprietor was told.
DECLARE CaveatFacts HAS
    `it discloses an estate or interest in land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it states the Government survey lot number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it affects only part of a lot` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it clearly identifies that part in an annexed plan` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is in fact justified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice was served by registered post on the proprietor and prior claimants` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since registration` IS A NUMBER
    `withdrawn by the caveator` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cancelled by order of court` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the caveat` IS A CaveatFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the caveat identifies the land adequately` IF
        `the caveat`'s `it states the Government survey lot number`
    AND (    NOT `the caveat`'s `it affects only part of a lot`
         OR  `the caveat`'s `it clearly identifies that part in an annexed plan`)

GIVEN `the caveat` IS A CaveatFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must refuse to register the caveat` IF
        NOT `the caveat`'s `it discloses an estate or interest in land`
    OR  NOT `the caveat identifies the land adequately` `the caveat`

-- The Registrar tests neither the merits nor the service of notice.
GIVEN `the caveat` IS A CaveatFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may refuse the caveat because the claim is unjustified` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `the caveat` IS A CaveatFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may refuse the caveat because notice was not served` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `the caveat` IS A CaveatFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the caveat is in force` IF
        `the caveat`'s `years since registration` LESS THAN 5
    AND NOT `the caveat`'s `withdrawn by the caveator`
    AND NOT `the caveat`'s `cancelled by order of court`

-- s 8(8): a later assurance in favour of the caveatee (given caveat) or the caveator (lodged caveat), conveying the
-- SAME estate or interest as protected by and so described in the subsisting caveat, presented and accepted while the
-- caveat is in force, when registered "has priority as though it had been registered on the date the caveat was
-- registered and that date is deemed to be the date of registration of the assurance for all purposes".
DECLARE LaterAssurance HAS
    `in favour of the person the caveat names or the person who lodged it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `conveys the same estate or interest as the caveat describes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `presented and accepted while the caveat was in force` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the later assurance` IS A LaterAssurance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the later assurance takes the caveat's date` IF
        `the later assurance`'s `in favour of the person the caveat names or the person who lodged it`
    AND `the later assurance`'s `conveys the same estate or interest as the caveat describes`
    AND `the later assurance`'s `presented and accepted while the caveat was in force`

-- The five years are measured from registration of the caveat, not from the date of the assurance.
-- An assurance presented the day after the caveat lapses gets no back-dating.

§§ `14 -- priority by registration date`

-- s 14(1): "all instruments registered under any repealed enactment, or entitled to be registered under this Act,
-- have priority according to the date of their registration and not according to the date of the instruments or of
-- their execution."
-- s 14(2): instruments registered on an identical date keep their priorities between themselves (the Act does not
-- change the existing order).
-- s 14(3): priorities "have full effect in all courts EXCEPT in cases of ACTUAL FRAUD, to which the person by or on
-- whose behalf the registration is made is a PARTY, ... and no such person loses any such priority merely in
-- consequence of the person having been affected with ACTUAL OR CONSTRUCTIVE NOTICE except in cases of actual fraud
-- to which the person is a party."
-- s 14(4): a person claiming without valuable consideration under another gets no further priority or protection than
-- the one they claim under; and "any disposition of land or charge on land which, if unregistered, would be
-- fraudulent and void is, despite registration, fraudulent and void in like manner."
DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `date of registration` IS A NUMBER
    `date of execution` IS A NUMBER
    `registered at the same moment as a competing instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person registering is a party to actual fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person registering had actual or constructive notice of the earlier interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `claims without valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `would be fraudulent and void if unregistered` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Who ranks first: the earlier REGISTRATION date, whatever the execution dates.
GIVEN `a` IS AN Instrument, `b` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first ranks ahead of the second by registration date` IF
    `a`'s `date of registration` LESS THAN `b`'s `date of registration`

-- Equal dates: the Act leaves the existing priority between them untouched.
GIVEN `a` IS AN Instrument, `b` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act determines priority between the two` IF
    NOT (`a`'s `date of registration` EQUALS `b`'s `date of registration`)

-- Priority is kept despite notice; it is lost only for actual fraud to which the registrant is a party.
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument keeps the priority its registration gives` IF
        NOT `the instrument`'s `the person registering is a party to actual fraud`
    AND NOT `the instrument`'s `would be fraudulent and void if unregistered`

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice of the earlier interest costs the instrument its priority` IF
        `the instrument`'s `the person registering had actual or constructive notice of the earlier interest`
    AND `the instrument`'s `the person registering is a party to actual fraud`

-- A volunteer takes no better position than the person they claim under.
GIVEN `the volunteer` IS AN Instrument, `the priority of the person claimed under is complete` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the volunteer enjoys full priority` IF
        `the instrument keeps the priority its registration gives` `the volunteer`
    AND (    NOT `the volunteer`'s `claims without valuable consideration`
         OR  `the priority of the person claimed under is complete`)

§§ `15 -- tacking further advances`

-- s 15(1): "Despite any other provision of this Act, a prior mortgagee of land has the right to make further advances
-- giving further credit or accommodation to rank in priority to subsequent mortgages -- (a) if the prior mortgage
-- AUTHORISES the making of further advances, or the giving of credit in instalments or on a current, revolving or
-- continuing account or other accommodation; or (b) where the prior mortgage does not expressly authorise ..., if the
-- SUBSEQUENT MORTGAGEE AGREES".
-- s 15(2): "Except as provided in this section, the right to tack does not apply to mortgages."
--
-- A "prior mortgage" includes a prior charge or assignment protected only by a caveat accepted for registration
-- (s 2(1)). The test is authorisation in the prior mortgage, or the subsequent mortgagee's consent. Notice that
-- further advances are being made, with no objection, is neither.
DECLARE Advance HAS
    `the advance is made by a prior mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the prior mortgage authorises further advances or revolving credit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the subsequent mortgagee agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the subsequent mortgagee merely knew and did not object` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the advance` IS AN Advance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the further advance ranks ahead of the subsequent mortgage` IF
        `the advance`'s `the advance is made by a prior mortgagee`
    AND (    `the advance`'s `the prior mortgage authorises further advances or revolving credit`
         OR  `the advance`'s `the subsequent mortgagee agreed`)

§§ `16 -- the purchaser's relief matches the seller's`

-- s 16: a person claiming under a duly registered assurance "has and is entitled to all the same grounds of relief" as
-- against anyone claiming through a later assurance which "has acquired priority by earlier registration", as the
-- person through whom they claim might have had.
GIVEN `the grantor could have obtained relief` IS A BOOLEAN, `the claimant claims under a duly registered assurance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant has the grantor's grounds of relief` IF
        `the grantor could have obtained relief`
    AND `the claimant claims under a duly registered assurance`
